\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Outcome and assignment conditions. All outcomes are $Y_i(z)=0.5x_i+z_i+s_i(z)+\epsilon _i$. Individual treatment is independent Bernoulli with probability $1/2$. The cluster condition changes assignment while retaining the strong-linear outcome mechanism. The recorded global effect is identical across the four families for each condition.}}{4}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:protocol}{{1}{4}{Outcome and assignment conditions. All outcomes are $Y_i(z)=0.5x_i+z_i+s_i(z)+\epsilon _i$. Individual treatment is independent Bernoulli with probability $1/2$. The cluster condition changes assignment while retaining the strong-linear outcome mechanism. The recorded global effect is identical across the four families for each condition}{table.caption.5}{}}
