\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Main results: mean cell RMSE and mean cell absolute bias, with 95\% paired seed-block percentile bootstrap intervals. Lower values are better. These are equal averages of cell summaries, not pooled errors over nodes or cells. Bias intervals include the nonlinearity of taking absolute seed-mean errors.}}{5}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{2}{5}{Main results: mean cell RMSE and mean cell absolute bias, with 95\% paired seed-block percentile bootstrap intervals. Lower values are better. These are equal averages of cell summaries, not pooled errors over nodes or cells. Bias intervals include the nonlinearity of taking absolute seed-mean errors}{table.caption.6}{}}
